# What Coolify builds on the VPS: nothing. It pulls the image GitHub Actions
# has already built and tested, the way astralco and kavre-scrap-yard do.
#
# The server has two cores and also runs Coolify, Traefik, Postgres and the
# other applications. Compiling here cost about a minute of both of those
# cores per deploy — 35 seconds of it the Go build alone, which began with an
# empty cache every time because no layer carries GOCACHE — and eight deploys
# in one morning is what spiked it.
#
# Coolify's build pack insists on building something, and BuildKit asks the
# registry for a tag on every build, so a lone FROM is how a build becomes a
# pull. The image brings its own entrypoint, health check, port and user, and
# FROM inherits all of them. Pass SOURCE_COMMIT to pin an exact commit rather
# than the newest image on main.
ARG SOURCE_COMMIT=latest
FROM ghcr.io/etherealfounder-al/nilami:${SOURCE_COMMIT}
